to invent new rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine putting those embeds and exploits into a lambda gadget for it to cover the entire area, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:53:37-07:00","id":470176,"title":"","content":"You could also just add a Bolthole trait that allows Demons to take their Demonic Forms inside the Bolthole without risking Compromise (maybe it uses the suborned Infrastructure idea from above, or the Cryptoflora one, whichever--or any--of them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:26:24-07:00","id":470238,"title":"","content":"Or the bar provides transition facades to demonic patrons prior to entry to prevent compromise. One does have to earn membership, providing Gerent with such a service, may well be one demon's ticket inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:36:29-07:00","id":470242,"title":"","content":"If I am recalling Heirs to Hell correctly, I believe Fractals can see straight through Covers. Not quite the Unchained doing it, but it's close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T16:37:26-07:00","id":470470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465514-what-does-it-take-for-demon-s-to-see-each-others-demonic-form?p=470242#post470242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am recalling Heirs to Hell correctly, I believe Fractals can see straight through Covers. Not quite the Unchained doing it, but it's close enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fractals can see through <i>their parents'</i> Covers, which is not quite the same level of extreme.<br /> <br /> There's a number of Mundane Embeds that could conceivably be mashed together to produce the effect of &quot;forces the target into their true form and prevents anyone from recognizing this as unusual,&quot; along with the possibility of Vocal Embeds keyed off of stifling realization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:44:14-07:00","id":470754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465514-what-does-it-take-for-demon-s-to-see-each-others-demonic-form?p=470470#post470470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fractals can see through <i>their parents'</i> Covers, which is not quite the same level of extreme.<br /> <br /> There's a number of Mundane Embeds that could conceivably be mashed together to produce the effect of &quot;forces the target into their true form and prevents anyone from recognizing this as unusual,&quot; along with the possibility of Vocal Embeds keyed off of stifling realization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? I could have sworn they could see through any demon cover. I can't remember the spot where it spells that out but I know for sure that a fractal in one of the short stories sees through a random group of demons it finds and they warn the demons of the coming danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:03:33-07:00","id":470790,"title":"","content":"It's kind of confusing because you have dissonance with the rules versus one of the chapter fictions. The rules say parents only. In the fiction, the Fractal lady sees the true forms of a ring of Demons in the same building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:44:45-07:00","id":470878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465514-what-does-it-take-for-demon-s-to-see-each-others-demonic-form?p=470754#post470754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? I could have sworn they could see through any demon cover. I can't remember the spot where it spells that out but I know for sure that a fractal in one of the short stories sees through a random group of demons it finds and they warn the demons of the coming danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tabbing through the PDF searching for &quot;cover&quot; only turns up two fairly unambiguous statements:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like Offspring, Fractals are stigmatics from birth. Additionally, they are born with an understanding of at least one Embed, <b>can see through their demon parents\u2019 Covers, </b>and usually have a few other innate talents that either mimic some of capabilities of their Unchained parents or allow them to achieve seemingly impossible feats (see Chapter Two). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fractal child is as much a danger to others as she is in danger herself, and that\u2019s a thing her parents know better than anyone. Those who do survive to adulthood tend to do it because their parents stuck with them regardless. <b>A part of that may be that Fractals have a much more intense connection to their parents than even the most sensitive Offspring. After all, a Fractal might see through all Covers and know what mommy really looks like, with her broken crown and bleeding wings.</b> </div> </div> </div>Tessa's perception of the demons in the OB/GYN ward could be explained as an ability similar to Quantum Understanding or as a drafting issue, but the point is that while it's possible to see through Cover it's nowhere near as simple as having the right easily-reproduced genetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:47:18-07:00","id":470899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465514-what-does-it-take-for-demon-s-to-see-each-others-demonic-form?p=470790#post470790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of confusing because you have dissonance with the rules versus one of the chapter fictions. The rules say parents only. In the fiction, the Fractal lady sees the true forms of a ring of Demons in the same building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe her conception was, uh, complicated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" 